Insert, Read, Update and Delete records in JDBC

Step 1: Create Table in MySQL.

CREATE DATABASE jdbc_db;
USE jdbc_db;
CREATE TABLE student 
(
    id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(50),
    marks INT
);

Step 2: 
JDBC Insert Program.

package jdbc;
                
import java.sql.Connection;           |
import java.sql.DriverManager;        |------ import java.sql.*;     
import java.sql.PreparedStatement;    |

public class InsertData
{
    public static void main(String[] args)
    {
        try
        {

            // Load Driver
            Class.forName("com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver");

            // Create Connection
            Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/jdbc_db", "root", "Root");

            // SQL Insert Query
            String query = "INSERT INTO student VALUES (?, ?, ?)";

            // Create PreparedStatement
            PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(query);

            // Set Values
            ps.setInt(1, 101);
            ps.setString(2, "Teju");
            ps.setInt(3, 85);

            // Execute Query
            int rows = ps.executeUpdate();

            // Output
            if(rows > 0)
            {
                System.out.println("Record Inserted Successfully");
            }

            // Close Connection
            con.close();
        }
        catch(Exception e)
        {
            System.out.println(e);
        }
    }
}

| Method                          | Purpose                             |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
|  Class.forName()                | Loads MySQL Driver                  |
|  DriverManager.getConnection()  | Connects Java with Database         |
|  prepareStatement()             | Creates SQL query object            |
|  setInt() ,  setString()        | Inserts values into query           |
|  executeUpdate()                | Executes INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE query |

Flow of JDBC Insert code :

Java Program
     ↓
Load Driver
     ↓
Create Connection
     ↓
Write INSERT Query
     ↓
Set Values
     ↓
Execute Query
     ↓
Data Stored in MySQL

